# The CFF schema requires the key "authors"; it lists the human contributor only (AI systems are
# named in the abstract and in formalization.yaml under automation).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "On sequential ideal measurements in the exceptional Jordan algebra: Lean 4 formalization"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "MacGregor"
    given-names: "Robert R."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1734-8054"
repository-code: "https://github.com/macgregor-sudo/albert-sequential-measurements"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - Albert algebra
  - exceptional Jordan algebra
  - sequential measurements
  - Lüders rule
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the papers "On sequential ideal measurements in the
  exceptional Jordan algebra" and "Finite certificates for sequential measurements in the
  exceptional Jordan algebra", version 2. Every numbered statement of the first paper is proved, and
  every numbered statement of the second except Remark 5.3, which is proved in part; twelve
  statements are compared with a Mathlib-only statement file by Comparator. The Albert algebra J = H3(O) is the 27-dimensional real Jordan
  algebra of 3x3 Hermitian octonionic matrices. An atom is an idempotent of trace one (a pure
  state). Its ideal yes-no test updates a state by the Lueders rule, and a word of outcomes has as
  probability the trace of the updated, unnormalised state. If finitely many atoms generate J, from
  any state no sequential projective representation on a real, complex or quaternionic Hilbert space
  reproduces all their word probabilities, and a finite linear inequality valid in every such
  representation fails by a positive margin from every state. Not generating J is equivalent to
  lying in a special unital subalgebra, and to one family of projections on C^6 or C^24 serving
  every state. For four generating atoms, from the maximally mixed state a representation on C^12
  reproduces every word of length at most six, but none every word of length at most seven. A
  polynomial A in thirteen traces is nonnegative for four atoms and positive exactly when they
  generate J; its maximum is 4/19683, and when A = 0 every state has a representation on C^6. Three
  atoms never generate J, and every state has a representation on C^3. The atoms are exactly the
  primitive idempotents. Except for the adapted code listed in docs/ATTRIBUTION.md (declarations
  adapted from Physlib, modules adapted from the contributor's Palomar entry
  PALOMAR-2026-10-16-000013, and composition-algebra modules adapted from
  ehrlich-b/composition-algebras), all mathematics, proofs, text and Lean code were produced by Claude
  Fable 5.2, Claude Opus 5.5, GPT-6.2 Astra, GPT-6.2 Sol, Gemini Carbon and Gemini Hydrogen; no
  human has reviewed the mathematics.
